  "limitations": [
    "Fresh both-root baseline precedes source reads: 460 records, 923 caches, 56 existing warnings, zero structural defects. Whole four records and all 14 original nodes/seven directions reviewed. Retain 12 nodes/three qualified existing directions; remove two workflow nodes/four context or coincidence arrows; rename seven nodes. No new topology or Edison spend.",
    "Tobacco and Artemisia whole indexed publisher abstracts/highlights read; MetG2 whole indexed abstract/Introduction and the displayed bounded experimental-design, metagenome, discussion/conclusion previews read. Chlorella whole independently retrieved EuropePMC abstract read, plus an indexed publisher preview lead. These are not complete papers. Direct ScienceDirect requests returned HTTP403; Crossref-advertised public API links for the two CC-licensed articles returned HTTP400. No bypass or whole-paper/supplement/figure-pixel/raw-data certification. Publisher index was crawled earlier; retrieval is fresh, not a claim that the publisher page was fetched live.",
    "Crossref version-of-record metadata identifies tobacco as CC BY4.0 and Artemisia as CC BY-NC4.0 despite local historical paywall wording. That metadata does not mean their complete bodies were retrieved. No cache or license949 repair is claimed. The four cited Markdown caches were read whole; Artemisia contains two trait/design sentences, not its full abstract. Existing cache content is unchanged and sufficient for every retained/new literal quotation.",
    "Tobacco: preserve measured substrate loss, community shifts and volatile/sensory outcomes. Remove mutualism and niche partitioning, qualify the existing directions and preserve PLS-PM mediation as a statistical hypothesis. No invented software/version, taxon-specific mediator or monoculture-synergy claim. Endpoint process annotations are removed because they describe upstream degradation, not volatile/sensory measurement.",
    "Chlorella: preserve 60-day removal, algal biomass/protein versus BG11 and transcript responses. Remove construction/duration nodes and three remaining noncausal arrows while preserving prior October2 repairs. No demonstrated cross-feeding, neutral bacterial fitness, isolated medium effect or measured metabolic flux. Only the algal observations gain canonical identity-only participant scope; unnamed bacterial membership remains existing issue183.",
    "MetG2: preserve microbial and host molecular responses and one qualified source-proposed functional contribution. Remove the context-only arrow, unestablished interaction types and redundant community-level source/target links. The indexed source names four inoculant strains and has a Chiliseed2/Chileseed2 spelling discrepancy; broad native rhizosphere Proteobacteria is not a resolved inoculant identity. Generic sugarcane is not verified as the canonical species. Record remains needs_research under1847; no new identifiers or canonical-taxonomy edits.",
    "Artemisia: preserve the pair-level tolerance, complementarity and PGP/carbon-fixation capacity. Remove niche partitioning and mutualism; source assay setting is not specified in the reviewed abstract, so OTHER replaces unsupported IN_VIVO assignment on these trait/design items. Preserve previous removal of screening-order arrows. Positive whole-abstract plant/soil outcomes are not rejected, but no new graph mechanism or sequestration-flux claim is introduced.",
    "Repair issues1843-1846 await protected-main merge; identity1847 and existing membership183 remain open. Fresh all-state issue titles/bodies and ignored/hidden local search matched1093,1091,184,183; all four bodies read. The122 local matching paths were inspected as an index, not all read; focused prior access/missing-PDF/author-request leads were inspected without contacting anyone. No reusable taxon match found in ignored/hidden-inclusive kb/taxa searches for the target names/IDs. PRs/comments not exhaustively searched.",
    "Only existing graphs, focused discussions and curation events change. All456 other records,923 caches, non-graph raw blocks and prior histories/decisions preserved. No schema, validator, runtime, census threshold or configuration changes. Non-graph membership, abundance, growth and role claims are not recertified. Loader1703, DOI-case1091 and stub-policy1093 remain separate. Self-review is not independent approval or corpus completion. Denied AM_AB000444 and unanswered Edison scopes untouched; validation/publication not preasserted."
  ]
